---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How ModusFi handles personal information when you visit its website or enquire about its services."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p>How we handle your personal information and respect your privacy.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <article class="container privacy-content" aria-label="Privacy notice">
      <p class="muted">
        Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-08">8 November 2026</time>
      </p>
      <p class="draft-note">
        Draft for launch. ModusFi is being incorporated; details marked for confirmation below
        remain under review.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This notice is prepared for ModusFi Software Technologies Limited, the company being
        established to operate ModusFi. Following incorporation, it will be responsible for the
        personal information described in this notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@modusfi.io">info@modusfi.io</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        This notice explains how we handle personal information when you visit modusfi.io, contact
        us or enquire about our services. Information about processing personal data when delivering
        client projects will be provided separately where appropriate.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you contact us, we collect your name, email address, message and any other information
        you choose to provide. We may also retain correspondence relating to your enquiry.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our website infrastructure and security services process technical information such as IP
        addresses, browser and device information, requested pages, timestamps and security signals.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please do not include passwords, account credentials or sensitive personal information in
        your enquiry.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we use your information</h2>
      <p>We use personal information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to enquiries and discuss our services.</li>
        <li>Take steps you request before entering into a contract with you.</li>
        <li>Operate and secure our website, prevent spam and investigate misuse.</li>
        <li>Handle privacy requests, complaints and applicable legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For general business enquiries and website security, we rely on our{' '}
        <strong>legitimate interests</strong> in communicating with prospective customers and
        protecting our services. We must balance these interests against your rights and interests.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where you personally request steps towards a contract with us, we may rely on{' '}
        <strong>steps necessary before entering into a contract</strong>. Where processing is
        required by law, we rely on the relevant <strong>legal obligation</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Providing enquiry information is voluntary, but we may be unable to respond without
        sufficient contact details.
      </p>

      <h2>Who receives your information</h2>
      <p>
        Access within ModusFi is restricted to authorised customer-services personnel and others who
        need it to handle your enquiry or meet our responsibilities.
      </p>
      <p>We use external services to operate the website and handle communications:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare:</strong> website hosting, network security and Turnstile spam
          protection.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Postmark:</strong> delivery of contact-form emails, when the integration is
          operational.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email mailbox provider:</strong> [To be confirmed before launch.]
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Fonts:</strong> delivery of the website’s fonts. Your browser connects to
          Google’s servers, which receive technical information including your IP address.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also disclose information to professional advisers or authorities where necessary for
        legal obligations or legal claims.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information or use contact-form submissions to enrol you in
        marketing campaigns.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>We do not currently use advertising or website analytics tools.</p>
      <p>
        We use Cloudflare Turnstile to distinguish legitimate visitors from automated traffic. It
        processes browser, device and network signals for security purposes. Further information is
        available in{' '}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">
          Cloudflare’s Turnstile Privacy Addendum
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p class="confirmation-note">
        [Confirm any cookies or browser storage used by the deployed Cloudflare configuration, their
        purposes and durations before publication.]
      </p>

      <h2>International processing</h2>
      <p>Some service providers may process personal information outside the United Kingdom.</p>
      <p class="confirmation-note">
        [Confirm the providers, relevant countries and applicable transfer arrangements. Identify
        the adequacy regulations or appropriate safeguards actually relied upon, and explain how
        visitors can obtain information about those safeguards.]
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>
        For enquiries that do not result in a client engagement, we retain correspondence for up to{' '}
        <strong>12 months after the last substantive contact</strong>, then delete it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where an enquiry becomes a client engagement, relevant information becomes part of the
        client record and is subject to the retention arrangements explained for that engagement.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may retain relevant information longer where necessary to meet a legal requirement or
        establish, exercise or defend legal claims.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on the circumstances, you may have rights to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access your personal information.</li>
        <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
        <li>Request deletion or restriction of its use.</li>
        <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interests.</li>
        <li>Receive certain information in a portable format.</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent where processing relies on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These rights are subject to applicable conditions and exceptions.</p>
      <p>
        Contact <a href="mailto:info@modusfi.io">info@modusfi.io</a> to exercise your rights. We may
        request proportionate information to verify your identity. We normally respond within one
        calendar month, subject to any extension or other provision permitted by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not use enquiry information to make solely automated decisions producing legal or
        similarly significant effects.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Please contact <a href="mailto:info@modusfi.io">info@modusfi.io</a> if you have a concern
        about how we handle personal information.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will acknowledge privacy complaints within 30 days, investigate them, keep you informed
        and communicate the outcome without undue delay.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office:{' '}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        We will update this notice when our activities or processing arrangements change. The date
        above indicates the latest revision.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-content {
    max-width: 850px;
    color: #43566b;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .privacy-content h2 {
    margin: 40px 0 16px;
    color: #101d32;
    font-family: 'Manrope', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 30px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .privacy-content p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .privacy-content ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 24px;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .privacy-content li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .privacy-content a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .privacy-content a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #00b3c6;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .draft-note,
  .confirmation-note {
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-left: 3px solid #00b3c6;
    background: #edf5fa;
  }
</style>
